  +
  +# Issues and the board: gh dojo
  +
  +This project tracks the issues of Trum-ok/gh-dojo on the GitHub Projects board Trum-ok/5, with the process in `.github/dojo.toml` (preset `kanban`). Take, move, comment on, block and create issues **only** through `gh dojo`: never change a status, a comment, a blocked-by link or an issue with `gh issue`, `gh project` or the API. For what gh dojo cannot do, such as editing an issue's title, body, labels or assignees, use `gh issue` only when the task needs it or the user asks.
  +
  +Start with `gh dojo describe`: the verbs, when to use each, what they need and do along the way, the lifecycle and the exit codes, read from the config without the network. `gh dojo <verb> --help` has the details of one verb. Read them rather than guess. When the setup is broken (token, board, config), `gh dojo doctor` names each problem with the command that fixes it.
  +
  +## Verbs
  +
  +Run a verb as `gh dojo <verb> N` (`N` or `#N`); `--dry-run` prints its plan (status, links, the comment it would post) without changing anything. A verb adds the issue to the board if it is missing and refuses a closed issue unless noted. It confirms in one line, such as `#42 Backlog → In progress, comment left`: there is no need to read the issue again.
  +
